/*
Detection Rule: Azure VM Extension Installed for Remote Code Execution
Author: Bryan Jorge
MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.004 - Command and Scripting Interpreter: Unix Shell
              T1546 - Event Triggered Execution
              T1505 - Server Software Component
Severity: Critical
Description: Detects the installation of VM extensions that can execute arbitrary
code on Azure virtual machines. VM extensions are a common attacker persistence
technique after gaining Azure subscription access — they provide durable RCE even
if the VM is rebooted, and run as SYSTEM/root. CustomScriptExtension, VMAccess,
and RunCommand extensions are the highest-risk types as they execute attacker-
controlled code or reset credentials directly on the machine.
*/

index=azure_activity sourcetype="azure:activity"
    operationName="Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/extensions/write"
    resultType="Success"

| eval actor=coalesce(caller, properties.caller, "unknown")
| eval vm_name=mvindex(split(resourceId, "/"), 8)
| eval resource_group=mvindex(split(resourceId, "/"), 4)
| eval subscription_id=mvindex(split(resourceId, "/"), 2)
| eval extension_name=mvindex(split(resourceId, "/"), -1)
| eval extension_type=spath(properties, "requestBody.properties.type")
| eval extension_publisher=spath(properties, "requestBody.properties.publisher")
| eval script_uri=spath(properties, "requestBody.properties.settings.fileUris")
| eval command_run=spath(properties, "requestBody.properties.settings.commandToExecute")
| eval has_protected_settings=if(
    isnotnull(spath(properties, "requestBody.properties.protectedSettings")), 1, 0)

/* Flag high-risk extension types capable of RCE or credential reset */
| eval is_rce_type=if(match(extension_type,
    "CustomScriptExtension|CustomScript|RunCommand|" .
    "VMAccessAgent|VMAccess|PowerShell|WindowsPowerShellDSC"),
    1, 0)

/* Flag scripts loaded from external (non-blob) URIs */
| eval is_external_script=if(
    isnotnull(script_uri) AND
    NOT match(script_uri, "blob\.core\.windows\.net"),
    1, 0)

/* Flag obfuscated commands commonly used to hide malicious payloads */
| eval is_obfuscated=if(
    match(command_run, "base64|iex |invoke-expression|-enc |-encoded|bypass|hidden"),
    1, 0)

| where is_rce_type=1 OR is_external_script=1

/* Score based on extension type, script origin, and obfuscation */
| eval risk_score=0
| eval risk_score=if(is_obfuscated=1 AND is_external_script=1,                  risk_score+70, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(is_external_script=1 AND is_rce_type=1,                    risk_score+60, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(is_obfuscated=1 AND is_rce_type=1,                         risk_score+55, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(extension_type, "VMAccessAgent|VMAccess"),            risk_score+50, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(is_external_script=1,                                       risk_score+40, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(is_rce_type=1,                                              risk_score+25, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(has_protected_settings=1,                                   risk_score+10, risk_score)

| stats
    count                        AS install_count,
    values(extension_type)       AS extension_types,
    values(extension_name)       AS extension_names,
    values(vm_name)              AS affected_vms,
    values(resource_group)       AS resource_groups,
    values(script_uri)           AS script_sources,
    values(command_run)          AS commands,
    values(sourceIPAddress)      AS actor_ips,
    min(_time)                   AS first_seen,
    max(_time)                   AS last_seen
    by actor, subscription_id, is_external_script, is_obfuscated, risk_score

| eval alert_title="Azure VM Extension RCE Backdoor Detected: " . actor
| table _time, alert_title, actor, extension_types, affected_vms,
        resource_groups, script_sources, commands, is_external_script,
        is_obfuscated, actor_ips, install_count, risk_score, first_seen, last_seen
| sort -risk_score

/*
TUNING PARAMETERS:
- extension_type whitelist: Add approved agent types to reduce noise from monitoring
  deployments (Log Analytics, Defender agents are commonly auto-deployed)
- is_external_script: Remove this condition if your org loads scripts from external CDNs
- Whitelist examples:
  | where NOT match(actor, "AzureAutomation|MicrosoftDefenderForCloud|AzurePolicy")
  | where NOT match(extension_type, "MicrosoftMonitoringAgent|OmsAgentForLinux|
    AzureMonitorLinuxAgent|DependencyAgentLinux")

FALSE POSITIVES:
- Azure Automation State Configuration deploying DSC configurations to managed VMs
- IT operations teams running CustomScript for approved patch or config deployment
- Azure Security Center / Defender for Servers auto-provisioning monitoring agents
- Packer or Terraform builds that install software via custom script during image creation

RECOMMENDED RESPONSE:
1. Verify whether the actor was authorized to install extensions on these VMs
2. Examine script URI content and command_run value for malicious indicators
3. Determine if this matches a scheduled automation runbook or change request
4. Remove the malicious extension: az vm extension delete --name <ext> --vm-name <vm>
5. Isolate the VM by applying a deny-all NSG rule to its NIC
6. Rotate SSH keys and local admin credentials for all affected VMs

INVESTIGATION QUERIES:
- Extension install history on affected VM: index=azure_activity
  operationName="Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/extensions/write"
  resourceId=*<vm_name>* | table _time, caller, properties
- Process activity via Defender (if Defender for Endpoint enrolled):
  DeviceProcessEvents | where DeviceName=~"<vm_name>" | project Timestamp, FileName,
  ProcessCommandLine, AccountName | order by Timestamp desc
- Network connections from VM: index=azure_nsg sourceIPAddress=<vm_ip> earliest=<first_seen>
  | stats count by destinationIPAddress, destinationPort, flowState

DATA SOURCES REQUIRED:
- Azure Activity Logs (ARM layer — extension write operations are captured here)
- Optional: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint logs for process-level correlation

HIGH-RISK INDICATORS:
- Script loaded from an external IP (not blob.core.windows.net) or unknown domain
- Command contains base64-encoded content (-enc flag, pipe to base64 -d)
- VMAccess extension used to reset SSH keys or local admin password (credential reset)
- Extension installed on multiple VMs across different resource groups simultaneously

PREVENTION MEASURES:
- Apply Azure Policy to restrict allowed VM extension publishers to an approved list
- Enforce Just-In-Time VM access to block ad-hoc extension installation by default
- Enable Microsoft Defender for Servers to detect malicious extension behavior at runtime
- Require approval via Azure DevOps or change management for all VM extension deployments

RELATED TECHNIQUES:
- T1078.004 - Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts
- T1098 - Account Manipulation
- T1053.003 - Scheduled Task/Job: Cron (persistence via user data / cloud-init)

CHANGELOG:
v1.0 (2026-02-17): Initial release
*/
